## Whitelisting commands inside `bash`

If you keep `bash` enabled, you can parse and whitelist commands. Simplest: allow only specific command prefixes:

```ts
const ALLOWED_BASH_PREFIXES = [
  "ls", "cat", "grep", "find", "git status", "git diff", "git log",
  "npm run", "npm test", "npx tsc --noEmit",
];

pi.on("tool_call", async (event, ctx) => {
  if (isToolCallEventType("bash", event)) {
    const cmd = event.input.command.trim();
    const allowed = ALLOWED_BASH_PREFIXES.some(p => cmd.startsWith(p));
    if (!allowed) {
      return { block: true, reason: `Command not in allowlist: ${cmd}` };
    }
  }
});
```

For better safety, parse with a shell parser or use a restricted execution environment rather than string matching.

